     "Saptarishi"
    ],
    "text": {
     "en": "A constellation is a group of stars that seems to form a pattern, like the Big Dipper (Saptarishi) or Orion. People gave them names from stories.\nThe Pole Star (Dhruva) stays almost fixed in the north, so travellers used it to find north. The Saptarishi pattern helps locate it.\nOther stars appear to move across the sky at night because the Earth rotates."
    }
